    <h2>A garden, seen from above</h2>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>The mark is a green disc with a J and a K cut out of it. The solid parts are the beds. The letters are the paths between them.</p>
      <p>So you don't really draw my initials. You walk them, which is roughly how this site works too: you wander from one idea to the next and see what's growing.</p>
      <p>The K's leg ends in a curl that turns back on itself and stops before it closes. That's my curly hair, and it's also a tendril still reaching for something. It stays open on purpose. Nothing here is finished.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>It took six tries</h2>
    <p class="prose" style="margin:0">Most of them were wrong in a useful way. Tap one to see it.</p>
