<section>
    <h2>What the garden is about</h2>
    <p class="prose" style="margin:0">Plants are the metaphor. These five are the point.</p>
    <ul class="traits">
      <li><h3>Curiosity</h3><p>Following an idea wherever it goes, including off the path.</p><p class="so"><b>So:</b> the logo is literally made of paths. Notes link to each other, and there's a map for wandering instead of navigating.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Care</h3><p>Tending thoughts instead of publishing them as finished opinions.</p><p class="so"><b>So:</b> every note carries two dates, planted and last tended. A yellow dot means I touched it in the last two weeks.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Growth</h3><p>Letting beliefs change, and leaving the evidence lying around.</p><p class="so"><b>So:</b> the curl in the mark never closes. Old notes go grey instead of disappearing.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Personality</h3><p>A real person behind it, with a family and a playlist.</p><p class="so"><b>So:</b> the mark is my initials, not a stock leaf. There's also an MP3 player like the one I had as a teenager.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Restraint</h3><p>Character without decorating every inch.</p><p class="so"><b>So:</b> one mark, one colour at a time, one loud thing per screen.</p></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="kicker">The line that started it</p>
    <div class="quote">
      <p class="deva" lang="hi">धीरे-धीरे रे मना, धीरे सब कुछ होय। माली सींचे सौ घड़ा, ऋतु आए फल होय।</p>
      <blockquote>Slowly, mind, everything happens slowly. The gardener pours a hundred pots of water, but <mark>fruit comes in its season</mark>.</blockquote>
      <p class="src">Kabir, 15th century</p>
      <p class="prose" style="margin:0">A hundred pots of water, and you still don't get to pick the day. That's how most of my ideas grow, so that's how the site works.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What it's made of</h2>
    <div class="made">
      <div>
